From: "JQE Chief Engineer (Claude)" <jqe-bot@example.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 22:28:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/37] fix: risk_controller.approve_trade accepts a real
 account balance
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Position sizing previously called calculate_position_size(balance=50,
...) — a hardcoded literal, completely ignoring the account's actual
balance regardless of caller. Adds a balance parameter (default 50,
preserving prior behavior for any caller that omits it) so callers can
pass a real balance (e.g. from BrokerGateway.get_account_info()). The
sizing formula itself is unchanged.

Also narrows a bare 'except Exception' around market_data.iloc[-1] to
the specific exceptions bad input can raise (AttributeError,
IndexError, TypeError), and cleans up formatting while touching the
file.

19 new tests covering every rejection branch, approval, and the
balance parameter's effect on lot sizing.
